Replace DPD collection-address toggle with a real whitelabel option, add
DPD connection reset (v0.109)

The v0.108 "don't send this address to DPD as the collection address"
toggle turned out not to achieve anything visible: leaving collectionDetails
off the request makes DPD fall back to the collection address configured on
the DPD account itself, which for a real account is still BNS's genuine
registered address. Confirmed against the full DPD shipping schema that
there is no API-level "hide the sender" flag at all - true white-labelling
is an account-level label template only DPD's own Customer Integration Team
can apply.

Replaced the toggle with "Whitelabel": when on, DPD is sent "-" for street
and town (the two address fields DPD actually content-validates) and the
country code is forced to GB, instead of the real Settings > DPD address.
Contact name/phone are left as configured, since DPD needs a real contact
for collection queries. As before, this only ever touches the domestic
collectionDetails block - the customs exporterDetails block on international
shipments is always sent with the real, complete address, since DPD rejects
those shipments outright otherwise.

Also added a "Reset DPD connection" button in the same Settings > DPD
section, after DPD support suggested resetting the connection / getting a
new bearer token to resolve an unrelated issue. Clears the cached
access/refresh token pair so the next DPD call re-authenticates from
scratch with the API key/secret, rather than refreshing or reusing the
existing session - the bearer token is that cached session token, separate
from and untouched by the API key/secret above.

